<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Amadeo I of Spain</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1845">1845</a>–<a href="/years/1890">1890</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Amadeo of Savoy</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Amadeo I, a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/victor-emmanuel-ii">Victor Emmanuel II</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, was elected King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/corte">Cortes</a> and reigned from 1871 to 1873. His backer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juan-prim">Juan Prim</a> was assassinated days before his arrival. Facing Carlist revolt, war in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuba">Cuba</a> and quarrelling parties, he abdicated in February 1873, and the First Spanish Republic was proclaimed.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/amadeo-i-of-spain.jpg" alt="Amadeo I of Spain" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pedro Martínez de Hebert · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Retrato-de-Amadeo-I-M-Hebert-Fot-Madrid_(1).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
